+  <p>On Windows, serve can take its certificate from the machine's certificate store instead, with the key left where it is (it is never read or exported): <code>-tls-thumbprint &lt;thumbprint&gt;</code> for one certificate, or <code>-tls-subject &lt;dns name&gt;</code> for the newest valid one that names the host in its Subject Alternative Name (a renewal is picked up within the hour, no restart), from <code>-tls-store</code> (default <code>LocalMachine\My</code>). A missing, expired or ambiguous certificate, or a key the account cannot open, stops serve with one line that says which. To let the account serve runs as read the key: <code>pgvigil cert -grant-key-access &lt;thumbprint&gt; -account DOMAIN\user</code> from an elevated prompt (Read only, to that one account; it prints the key's old access list first), or certlm.msc &gt; the certificate &gt; All Tasks &gt; Manage Private Keys.</p>
   <p>Adding servers, the SQL Server login, the cloud settings and every option are in the <a href="https://github.com/aachaemenes/pgvigil#readme">documentation</a>. For a site with no internet access, follow the <a href="https://github.com/aachaemenes/pgvigil/blob/main/docs/airgap.md">offline install</a>. To move an installed pgvigil to a new release, follow the <a href="https://github.com/aachaemenes/pgvigil/blob/main/docs/upgrade.md">upgrade</a> in its order.</p>
